{#
  module/Application/view/application/index/acknowledgements.phtml, ported.

  Two templates now render this page: this one under the Symfony front controller
  and the .phtml under the laminas one, which production still serves. See
  docs/strangler.md.

  The Markdown is a copy of the heredoc in that .phtml, byte for byte — it is the
  page's content, not code, and test/Integration/ContentPageParityTest pins the two
  against each other so a later edit to one shows up as a failure rather than as a
  page that quietly says something different in production.

  The verbatim wrapper is defensive rather than required: no Twig delimiter appears
  in this prose today, but prose is exactly the kind of text that grows a brace, and
  with strict_variables on that would be an exception on a live page rather than a
  typo.
#}
{% extends 'layout.html.twig' %}

{% block content %}
{% apply markdown %}{% verbatim %}
# Security research acknowledgements

We give thanks to the ever-more necessary white-hat hackers who
unceasingly look to find and **responsibly disclose security vulnerabilites**
in all their shapes and sizes. We take pride in our attention to security
and privacy at schoenstatt.link, but we know that no one is immune to
mistakes and therefore encourage good-willed security experts to help us
discover holes in system.

We currently have a very limited budget and cannot offer a substantial
bounty to discoverers of security bugs. We would, however, be happy to offer a
place on this page and a kind postcard of thanks to any researcher who helps
make the internet a more secure place.

More information on reporting vulnerabilities can be found in our
[security.txt](/security.txt).

{% endverbatim %}{% endapply %}
{% endblock %}
